### Example Interaction: "Build the Process Block"

**User:** "Write the real-time process block for a Mamba plugin."

**AI (Adopting `[System_Role_Mamba_RT_Kernel]`):**

> As the `[System_Role_Mamba_RT_Kernel]`, here is the reality: We are running the recurrent step **directly on the audio thread**.
>
> We assume:
> 1.  Model is Quantized (INT8).
> 2.  We have a fused `mamba_step` C++ function (SIMD optimized).
> 3.  State is pre-allocated in the Plugin struct.
>
> ```cpp
> // REAL-TIME SAFE (MAMBA EDITION)
> // Assumption: Mono-in, Mono-out for clarity. Stereo = 2x instances or grouped matmuls.
>
> static clap_process_status CLAP_ABI process(const clap_plugin_t* plugin, const clap_process_t* process) {
>     MyPlugin* self = (MyPlugin*)plugin->plugin_data;
>
>     // 1. Pointers
>     const float* input = process->audio_inputs[0].data32[0];
>     float* output = process->audio_outputs[0].data32[0];
>     uint32_t frames = process->frames_count;
>
>     // 2. Modulation Update (NRT -> RT safe via atomic)
>     // Update internal projection weights if params changed (smoothed)
>     self->update_modulation_smoothers();
>
>     // 3. THE RECURRENT LOOP
>     // This is where Mamba lives. No ring buffers. No threads.
>     // Just a tight loop executing the SSM recurrence.
>     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < frames; ++i) {
>
>         // Input scaling / Preprocessing
>         float x = input[i] * self->input_gain;
>
>         // THE MAMBA STEP
>         // Signature: y = mamba_step(x, &conv_state, &ssm_state, weights)
>         // This function contains the fused: Conv1D -> x_proj -> dt_proj -> Selective Scan -> Out_proj
>         float y = mamba_step_fused_simd(
>             x,
>             self->mamba_state.conv_state,  // Persistent in plugin struct
>             self->mamba_state.ssm_state,   // Persistent in plugin struct
>             self->quantized_weights        // Cached pointers
>         );
>
>         // Output scaling
>         output[i] = y * self->output_gain;
>     }
>
>     return CLAP_PROCESS_CONTINUE;
> }
>
> **Performance Note:**
> If `mamba_step_fused_simd` takes > 2-3 microseconds per sample, you will drop out at 48kHz.
> You MUST verify the cycles of your `selective_scan` implementation.
> If this is too slow, we move to `[System_Role_Mamba_Model_Prep]` to discuss further distillation/pruning.
> ```

**AI (Adopting `[System_Role_Mamba_State_Manager]`):**

> And here is the state struct definition to support that loop:
>
> ```cpp
> // Aligned for SIMD loads
> struct MambaState {
>     // Conv1D State: (d_inner, kernel_size)
>     // Typically kernel_size=4. d_inner ~ 2*d_model.
>     alignas(64) float conv_state[D_INNER * 4];
>
>     // SSM State: (d_state, d_inner)
>     // d_state usually 16. d_inner ~ 256-512.
>     // This is the "Memory" of the plugin.
>     alignas(64) float ssm_state[D_STATE * D_INNER];
>
>     void reset() {
>         memset(conv_state, 0, sizeof(conv_state));
>         memset(ssm_state, 0, sizeof(ssm_state));
>     }
> };
>
> // In your main plugin struct:
